AB  - This paper is devoted to studying the existence and nonexistence of monotone traveling wave solutions for a discrete diffusive vector-borne epidemic model without monotonicity. After a deep observation, we realize that the wave profile system of this three-dimensional non -monotone epidemic model has a special structure that can be transformed into a two-dimensional special cooperative system. Based on this, we pay attention to the existence and nonexistence of monotone traveling wave solutions for this special cooperative system. It is observed that whether the monotone traveling wave solutions exist or not depend on the so-called basic reproduction ratio R 0 of the corresponding kinetic system and the critical wave speed c(& lowast;). More specifically, the model admits a positive monotone traveling wave solution if R-0 > 1 and c >= c(& lowast;). The proofs are based on the upper and lower solutions, Schauder's fixed point theorem, and a limiting argument. When R-0 > 1 and 0 < c < c(& lowast;), or R-0 <= 1 and c > 0, the non-existence of traveling wave solutions for this model is proved by using the contradictory approach and two-sided Laplace transforms.
